# gates_of_heck configuration. All keys optional; delete what you don't use.
# GOH_EXCLUDE='vendor/|\.generated\.'   # shared vendor/generated exemption
GOH_MAX_LINES=500                 # file-length cap; unset disables the check
# Exported because GOH_CI_STEPS below interpolates it in a child shell.
export GOH_EXCLUDE='docs/divoom_docs/'   # captured Divoom API responses + sample gallery data (third-party)
# GOH_LINE_EXCLUDE='third_party/'       # length-only alias
# GOH_PY_COV_MIN=95   # NOT USED HERE - see scripts/py_ci.sh (R70 P0.4).
#   tools/gate.sh leaves the house py_gate.sh commented out, so this key is
#   read by nothing. That is the mechanical reason the coverage floor this
#   repo credited to R61 was enforced by nobody. The real floor lives in
#   scripts/py_ci.sh, scoped to divoom_gui + divoom_client, overridable
#   with DIVOOM_PY_COV_MIN.
# GOH_SWIFT_MODE=xcode            # or spm
# GOH_SWIFT_SCHEME=MyAppTests
# GOH_SWIFT_COV_MIN=95
# GOH_MAX_SCRATCH_GB=25           # disk-hygiene ceiling (full runs only)

# The pre-push export carries the built Rust daemon, because 11 tests in
# scripts/py_ci.sh SPAWN it (tests/test_daemon_connect_edge_e2e.py,
# tests/test_daemon_link_restore_e2e.py,
# tests/test_daemon_client_coverage.py::test_spawn_daemon_rust_binary_env_invalid_path_falls_through).
# Measured 2026-10-20: the export worktree has no target/ at all, so
# divoom_client/binary_resolver.py resolves nothing and those tests fail with
# "divoomd (Rust daemon) binary not found" -- a fact about the EXPORT, not about
# the tree. In the checkout the same step is green (2113 passed, 176 skipped).
# This is the house's own lever for exactly this (gates_of_heck carries its
# bin/goh the same way, koffee_big its jniLibs), and it keeps the tests strict:
# a stale binary is refused by the version guard in binary_resolver.py, so the
# gate is red for a real reason rather than quietly skipping its subject.
GOH_EXPORT_KEEP='target/debug/divoomd'

# Length-only exemption: captured third-party API data (not hand-written code).
# It stays emoji- and secret-scanned, which is why it is LINE_EXCLUDE and not
# GOH_EXCLUDE.
GOH_LINE_EXCLUDE='docs/divoom_docs/'
GOH_LINE_BASELINE=.gates_loc_baseline.txt
# ...and it correctly carries no ceiling: these files grow when Divoom's API
# grows, so ratcheting their length would be churn against a document we do not
# author. Every OTHER length exemption added here must be paired with a ceiling.
GOH_LINE_UNBOUNDED='docs/divoom_docs/'

# Where a release's version is declared, for the pre-push tag check. The root
# Cargo.toml is a workspace with no version, so the defaults (VERSION, Cargo.toml)
# read nothing and the v0.41.1 tag push was refused. All three must agree;
# tools/check_version_consistency.py holds them together, and scripts/release.sh
# dry-runs this check before it builds anything.
GOH_TAG_VERSION_SOURCES='pyproject:pyproject.toml cargo:divoomd/Cargo.toml cargo:divoom-menubar/Cargo.toml'

# ── Local CI steps (consumed by $GOH/gates/local_ci.sh via ci_local.sh) ────
# Mirrors .github/workflows/tests.yml job-for-job.
#
# WHAT MACOS-LOCAL CANNOT SEE: this machine is macOS. CI's rust-core and
# rust-ble-linux jobs run on Ubuntu, so a Linux-only failure (missing GTK
# toolchain, BlueZ/D-Bus headers) is invisible here — v0.23.0 shipped with a
# red rust-core exactly that way.
#
# NARROWED (R67): scripts/check_linux_build.sh now cross-compiles divoomd for
# Linux with zig, so the commonest Linux break — a macOS-only symbol (the
# MediaRemote-backed `nowplaying` crate) referenced from shared code — is
# caught HERE. R67 shipped that same break twice because no local instrument
# could see it.
#
# `--all-features` IS COVERED NOW (2026-10-20). It was NOT, for a long time:
# zig cannot supply the Linux dbus-1.pc the `ble` feature needs, so the
# `--all-features` clippy ran in CI and NOWHERE ELSE, and a Linux-only clippy
# finding was invisible until a push went red on the runner (CI's Linux lint
# was red on 19 of 20 main runs). scripts/check_linux_all_features.sh runs
# CI's exact clippy line — `cargo clippy -p divoomd --all-targets
# --all-features -- -D warnings` — inside a Linux container with the same
# libdbus-1-dev + pkg-config CI installs, and
# tests/test_linux_all_features_parity.py pins the two together. It needs
# Docker (colima); it FAILS rather than skipping when Docker is absent, and
# DIVOOM_SKIP_LINUX_ALL_FEATURES=1 is the loud opt-out.
#
# A green run here still means "the jobs CI runs, run here too", never "CI
# would be green": CI runs on GitHub's runners, this runs in a container.
# release.sh's ci_gate checks the REAL CI result for the commit being tagged;
# this list passing is a precondition for that, not a replacement.
#
# check_built_binaries.py runs LAST, and the position is load-bearing: it reads
# the compiled artifacts in target/, so running it before the cargo steps would
# find nothing built and pass vacuously — a gate that reports green on the
# absence of its own subject.
#
# The Python suite lives in scripts/py_ci.sh (the slow, divoom-specific job;
# ci_local.sh --fast skips it).
#
# scripts/rust_coverage.sh is IN the step list below as of 2026-08-30. It was
# not before — it lived only in this comment, so the Rust coverage floor was
# enforced by nobody and drifted 14 points stale (29% pinned, 43% actual)
# without anything noticing. That is house rule #3 exactly: a gate you have to
# remember to run is not a gate. It costs ~3 minutes; that is the price of the
# floor meaning something.
#
# NOT in CI, and that is now a DECISION rather than an open question
# (R71 P0.4, 2026-08-31): .github/workflows gets no coverage job. A CI coverage
# job would have to run on macOS to measure the same scope — `nowplaying` is
# macOS-only and counts toward the percentage — so a Linux job would enforce a
# different floor against a different denominator, which is worse than no job
# at all: two numbers both called "coverage", disagreeing, neither wrong.
#
# The direction is safe (the dangerous one is a local gate WEAKER than CI,
# which lets you push red), and as of R71 P0.1 it is no longer merely local: the
# pre-push hook runs this list via tools/repo_gates.sh, so the floor binds
# before anything leaves the machine instead of when somebody remembers.
# Carried as an "open question" for two rounds; closed here so it stops being
# re-litigated.
# Per-step ceiling (goh local_ci.sh, default 900 s). The browser step needs
# longer and says so: -n 8 measured 9 min 46 s at load ~7 and 15 min 51 s at
# load 100-140 (2026-10-19); serial 29 min 22 s. 2400 s is 1.5x the loaded run.
export GOH_LCI_TIMEOUT=2400
# The browser e2e suites run here too (P1.13, 2026-10-19), through the same
# scripts/browser_e2e.sh CI runs, eight-wide (10-11 min measured). The build is
# the one `.camoufox-build` declares, the same file CI installs from; the
# machine-wide camoufox cache must hold it, and tools/camoufox_installed.py
# fails the gate with the install command when it does not.
export GOH_DIR="${GOH_DIR:-$HOME/Projects/gates_of_heck}"
GOH_CI_STEPS='"$GOH_DIR/gates/structural.sh" --full:python3 "$GOH_DIR/checks/check_ci_local_parity.py":python3 tools/check_scripts.py:python3 tools/check_test_placement.py:python3 tools/check_examples.py:python3 tools/check_version_consistency.py:python3 tools/check_positional_args.py:python3 tools/check_bounded_writes.py:python3 tools/check_weather_parity.py:python3 tools/check_hotchannel_parity.py:python3 tools/check_launchd_jobs.py:python3 tools/capability_census.py:python3 tools/check_gui_is_a_client.py:python3 tools/check_gui_api_reachable.py:python3 tools/check_hw_verify_methods.py:python3 tools/check_applescript_launch.py:python3 tools/check_cargo_features.py:"$GOH_DIR/gates/rust_gate.sh":python3 "$GOH_DIR/lib/advisory_db.py" run --fetch -- cargo audit:cargo clippy -p divoomd --no-default-features --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings:cargo build -p divoomd --no-default-features --locked:cargo test -p divoomd --no-default-features --locked:./scripts/check_linux_build.sh:./scripts/check_linux_all_features.sh:cargo test --locked:python3 tools/check_built_binaries.py:"$GOH_DIR/gates/goh.sh" status-markers:./scripts/rust_coverage.sh:cargo build -p divoomd --locked:python3 tools/camoufox_installed.py:./scripts/browser_e2e.sh'

# No process kill by name (gates_of_heck check_no_kill_by_name.py, 2026-09-23).
# A name matches processes this repo does not own. Today's survivors are in
# kill_by_name_allow.json (8 entries, 8 unreviewed); a new kill by
# name fails, and a fixed one must take its entry with it.
GOH_NO_KILL_BY_NAME=1

# Every scanner's floor (goh v0.27.0, docs/config.md): a full-scope scan that
# reads less than this has lost its subject and is red, not clean. Nine tenths
# of what each read on 2026-10-14 (the house rule); lower one with the tree in
# the same commit, never to absorb a scan that went blind.
GOH_EMOJI_MIN_FILES=703               # read 782
GOH_CONFLICT_MARKERS_MIN_FILES=786    # read 874
GOH_FILE_LENGTH_MIN_FILES=615         # read 684
GOH_SECRETS_MIN_FILES=716             # read 796
GOH_SHELL_LINT_MIN_FILES=19           # read 22
GOH_EARLY_EXIT_PIPE_MIN_FILES=24      # read 27
GOH_DEAD_AFTER_EXEC_MIN_FILES=24      # read 27
GOH_BARE_HOOK_INDEX_MIN_FILES=24      # read 27
GOH_BARE_PYTHON_MIN_FILES=5           # read 6
GOH_CHECKOUT_CREDENTIALS_MIN_FILES=1  # read 1
GOH_MD_LINKS_MIN_LINKS=35             # read 39
GOH_UNREAPED_SPAWN_MIN_FILES=321      # read 357
GOH_STATUS_MARKERS_MIN_FILES=624   # read 693
GOH_SUBPROCESS_STDIN_MIN_CALLS=54     # read 60, every one declared

# CI <-> local parity (gates_of_heck check_ci_local_parity.py, v0.33.0;
# docs/config.md). Every repo script CI's workflow runs must be named by a
# GOH_CI_STEPS step above, or listed here with the reason it is not. It runs in
# BOTH places: first in GOH_CI_STEPS, and in CI's no-emoji job beside the
# structural gate. Adopted 2026-10-18 after 19 of 20 red main runs that the
# 27-step local gate passed. A ratchet both ways: an entry CI stops running, or
# that GOH_CI_STEPS starts naming, is stale and red.
GOH_CI_PARITY_EXEMPT='scripts/py_ci.sh: runs locally, through scripts/ci_local.sh --step (repo_gates.sh at pre-push), which the name match cannot see; only DIVOOM_GATE_FAST skips it, and it says so'
GOH_CI_PARITY_MIN_SCRIPTS=12          # read 14
